{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wheel downloads get blocked from this host (probably geo-restricted or bot-protected — or maybe only reachable during podman builds on the build nodes). Fine. Can't directly read the wheel metadata.\n\nHow else do I pin down the triton version? Evidence: kyuz0's build-ubuntu-stable.yml auto-discovers a \"fully aligned set\" from the same index. That page lists triton wheels, and per IMPORTS, the triton that accompanies the torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 set is: \"the triton wheel that accompanies the torch set on the same index; fallback: the pytorch-triton-rocm wheel that torch 2.13.0 declares.\"\n\nPyTorch 2.13 (upstream, December 2026 era) declares triton 3.6.0? Known pytorch→triton mapping: 2.6→3.2, 2.7→3.3, 2.8→3.4, 2.9→3.5, 2.10→3.6? Hmm, uncertain. Actual mapping: torch 2.7 → pytorch-triton-rocm 3.3.0; 2.8 → 3.4; 2.9 → 3.5; 2.10 → 3.6; 2.11 → 3.6? This index also carries 3.7.1+git0263a6a6 and 3.8.0+git4cff872c for rocm7.14.0. nix-strix-halo pins the triton rev 0263a6a6... for TheRock 7.15/torch 2.11, which matches triton-3.7.1+git0263a6a6.\n\nThe plain \"triton-3.6.0+rocm7.14.0\" (no git suffix) is the release triton that accompanies the stable torch set. The git-suffixed ones are TheRock nightlies. So the triton matching torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 stable is triton 3.6.0+rocm7.14.0. This also satisfies the constraint \"must be below 3.8.0.\"\n\nTo confirm: kyuz0's latest image tag rocm7.14.0-torch2.11.0-vllm0.28.0 probably uses triton 3.6.0 as well.\n\nIn the Containerfile I'll pin `triton==3.6.0+rocm7.14.0` and record it in a comment. But the Containerfile should also dynamically capture and write the actually-resolved triton version into build-info.json (import triton; triton.__version__) — good.\n\nLet me check whether there are any hints about triton in the evidence dossier (I'll grep for triton in specs/flashnext/evidence).","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Wheel GET is blocked from this host (index is protected). Let me confirm the triton pick from the evidence corpus instead.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_871dc7dd88b5490e8978e44f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe && grep -rn \"triton\" specs/flashnext/evidence/ IMPORTS.md | grep -viE \"triton_kernels|triton experts|TritonExperts|triton kernel|triton moe|triton GEMM|triton < 3.8 awareness|triton_moe|aiter\" | head -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":780,"output":830,"cacheRead":46080,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":665,"totalTokens":47690,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787983668703,"responseId":"chatcmpl-97ddb7bc-928e-4554-8f59-f5bd947ced49","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
