{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait: inside a RUN with heredoc — `RUN mkdir -p /opt/flashnext && python3 - <<'PY' \\ && cat ...` — this backslash continuation line followed by `&& cat` doesn't work: the heredoc consumes up to PY, and the `&& cat` line after PY… Actually, I wrote `python3 - <<'PY' \\`, then the python lines, then `PY`, then `&& cat`? No — I wrote `\\` at the end of the `python3 - <<'PY'` line, followed by the heredoc content, then `PY`, then… looking at my file: the RUN line ends with `<<'PY' \\`, followed by the python code, and `PY` closes the heredoc. The backslash after <<'PY' continues the shell command line — so the next line becomes part of the same shell command line… but it's also the start of the heredoc content. The heredoc content begins after the newline of the command line. The trailing `\\` escapes the newline, so does the shell concatenate the next line?? Heredoc semantics: `python3 - <<'PY' \\` — the backslash+newline is a line continuation in the shell's command word parsing, and the heredoc body begins from the line after the complete command line (after continuation processing? actually the heredoc body begins from the next line after the newline that terminated the command — if that newline is escaped by `\\`, the command continues and the heredoc body begins later). This is fragile/wrong. Let's restructure: no backslash; put `&& cat` before the heredoc? Impossible — cat after python completes: the structure is:\n\n```\nRUN mkdir -p /opt/flashnext \\\n && python3 - <<'PY'\n...python...\nPY\nRUN cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json\n```\nHeredoc inside Dockerfile RUN: does the shell-form RUN support heredocs in buildah/docker (via /bin/sh -c \"...\" as a single string)? Does Docker classic pass the RUN line as separate logical lines? Dockerfile RUN shell form: everything up to the next instruction is one command string joined by newlines; heredocs work with BuildKit and buildah (sh gets the complete script including newlines). The classical issue: Dockerfile parsers before BuildKit treated RUN as continuing only with backslashes; heredoc bodies were included as part of the command (newline-separated lines are part of the RUN command until the next instruction keyword). Yes — lines until the next Dockerfile instruction are part of the RUN command, so heredocs work in buildah.\n\nTherefore:\n\n```\nRUN mkdir -p /opt/flashnext && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ...\nPY\nRUN cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json\n```\n\nAlso rocm-sdk-core: does pip install name the distribution \"rocm-sdk-core\"? The wheel is rocm_sdk_core-7.14.0; importlib.metadata.version(\"rocm-sdk-core\") — the normalized name is \"rocm-sdk-core\" ✓. However, if torch's dependencies pull it in automatically — no problem, it should exist. If not (does torch bundle _rocm_sdk_core internally?), md.version will throw an exception. In the evidence, the runtime image references `_rocm_sdk_core` as a package in site-packages. But what is the installed distribution name? Could it be a `_rocm_sdk_core` provided by the torch wheel? According to the kyuz0 evidence, torch \"ships its own matched ROCm (_rocm_sdk_core)\", and the index has a separate rocm-sdk-core wheel. Torch's Requires-Dist is probably rocm-sdk-core==7.14.0. Keep it, but be defensive: use a try/except returning \"unknown\"? For the honesty of the receipt, better to keep the hard version retrieval for torch/triton and the defensive retrieval for rocm_sdk_core. Make it defensive.\n\nLet's fix the Containerfile's RUN block.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I need to fix the heredoc RUN block (the trailing backslash breaks heredoc parsing):\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_115be0b7c4a94660890bb671","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe/container/Containerfile","edits":[{"oldText":"RUN mkdir -p /opt/flashnext && python3 - <<'PY' \\\n    && cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json\nimport json, time, importlib.metadata as md\ninfo = {\n    \"lane\": \"container\",\n    \"image\": \"flashnext:dev\",\n    \"fork_repo\": \"https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm\",\n    \"fork_branch\": open(\"/opt/flashnext-fork-commit\").read().splitlines()[1],\n    \"fork_commit\": open(\"/opt/flashnext-fork-commit\").read().splitlines()[0],\n    \"torch\": md.version(\"torch\"),\n    \"torchvision\": md.version(\"torchvision\"),\n    \"triton\": md.version(\"triton\"),\n    \"rocm_sdk_core\": md.version(\"rocm-sdk-core\"),\n    \"gpu_target\": \"gfx1151\",\n    \"built_at\": time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z\"),\n}\njson.dump(info, open(\"/opt/flashnext/build-info.json\", \"w\"), indent=1)\nPY","newText":"RUN mkdir -p /opt/flashnext && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, time, importlib.metadata as md\ndef ver(name):\n    try:\n        return md.version(name)\n    except md.PackageNotFoundError:\n        return \"unknown\"\nlines = open(\"/opt/flashnext-fork-commit\").read().splitlines()\ninfo = {\n    \"lane\": \"container\",\n    \"image\": \"flashnext:dev\",\n    \"fork_repo\": \"https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm\",\n    \"fork_commit\": lines[0],\n    \"fork_branch\": lines[1] if len(lines) > 1 else \"flashnext\",\n    \"torch\": md.version(\"torch\"),\n    \"torchvision\": md.version(\"torchvision\"),\n    \"triton\": md.version(\"triton\"),\n    \"rocm_sdk_core\": ver(\"rocm-sdk-core\"),\n    \"gpu_target\": \"gfx1151\",\n    \"built_at\": time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z\"),\n}\njson.dump(info, open(\"/opt/flashnext/build-info.json\", \"w\"), indent=1)\nPY\nRUN cat /opt/flashnext/build-info.json"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":5023,"output":1500,"cacheRead":59136,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":845,"totalTokens":65659,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":178798399