{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Excellent — it got resolved empirically: **torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0**. So the corresponding triton is 3.8.0+git4cff872c, not 3.7.1. But IMPORTS says \"needs to be aware of < 3.8.0: the fork's fp8-upcast gate is keyed on triton < 3.8.\" Hmm — if triton 3.8.0 is the exact corresponding wheel for torch 2.13.0, then the fp8-upcast gate `on_gfx1151() and triton < 3.8` evaluates to FALSE at runtime on this substrate, and the upcast won't happen!\n\nWait — this is an important finding. Options:\n1. Pin triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0 and install torch with --no-deps (or install triton first and then install torch, tolerating pip's conflict warning). But \"don't loosen anything: the torch pin must be exactly satisfied\" — the torch pin is satisfied; triton is a separate wheel. Installing torch in a state where pip warns about the dependency conflict… does pip install fail if you later install a conflicting package? Order: install triton 3.7.1 first, then `pip install torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 torchvision...` — pip checks the dependencies of the torch being installed: requires triton==3.8.0... → ResolutionImpossible again, because it validates against the installed environment. Workaround: first install torch alone with --no-deps… but then torch's other dependencies (rocm-sdk-core, sympy, networkx, etc.) won't be installed. Alternative: run `pip install --no-deps torch==... torchvision==... triton==3.7.1...`, then `pip install` the remaining runtime dependencies… but the list of torch's dependencies is unclear.\n\nHmm. Which is correct for the campaign? IMPORTS.md is authoritative: \"triton | wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index; fallback: the pytorch-triton-rocm wheel declared by torch 2.13.0 | same index | needs to be aware of < 3.8.0: the fork's fp8-upcast gate is keyed on triton < 3.8 (see PR #52970 pattern). Record the resolved version in the build receipt.\"\n\n\"The wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index\" — for torch 2.13.0, what AMD publishes as the corresponding wheel is 3.8.0+git4cff872c (which pip just proved). But then the gate `triton < 3.8` kills the fp8 upcast. Could it be that… the fork's gate is keyed on `triton < 3.8`, and 3.8.0+git4cff872c is parsed as version 3.8.0 → not less than 3.8. Hmm, so admission happens but the upcast is OFF? The admission patch approves the scheme; the upcast kernel transform is gated on triton<3.8. With triton 3.8, the kernel might work natively (does tl.dot support fp8 on newer triton? On RDNA3.5 there's no FP8 unit — the upcast exists because older triton lowers fp8 tl.dot incorrectly; newer triton might handle it fine, or AMD's triton might still need the upcast).\n\nWait, re-reading: \"the fork's fp8-upcast gate is keyed on triton < 3.8 (see PR #52970 pattern).\" #52970 applies the upcast when on_gfx1151 and triton < 3.8 — meaning in triton ≥ 3.8 the fp8 dot is properly handled in software? That's the upstream understanding: ROCm triton 3.8 got correct fp8 emulation on RDNA3.5? So the corresponding set (torch 2.13 + triton 3.8.0+git4cff872c) is coherent: with triton 3.8, the gate intentionally skips the upcast.\n\nBut wait — does the fork's patch still approve the MOE scheme on gfx1151 regardless of triton version? Yes, the approval is keyed on gfx1151; the upcast is conditioned on triton<3.8 (on 3.8, the fp8 dot path is assumed to be correct).\n\nHmm, but with the triton 3.8 wheel on RDNA3.5, is `tl.dot` on fp8 inputs actually numerically sound? That's UNKNOWN-1, and we resolve it via the proxy + fidelity checkpoint. The campaign spec/IMPORTS accepts the corresponding set; the gate handles both regimes.\n\nDecision: use the exact corresponding set that pip resolved: triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0. This is \"the wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index\" and satisfies torch's own declaration — the most defensible \"don't loosen anything\" stance. Record it in the receipt and comment about the < 3.8 awareness: at 3.8.0 the fork's upcast gate is false, and the approved fp8 dot goes through triton's own lowering; if fidelity is broken, it's UNKNOWN-1 territory.\n\nNo wait — one more consideration. If the upcast doesn't fire, then \"admission patch + upcast\" (world-first piece) goes untested… but that's campaign semantics beyond my task; my task: exact corresponding set, record the resolved version. The smoke receipt logs the admission verdict (approval), and that should pass.\n\nHmm, but hold on — could it be that the intent of IMPORTS was to choose triton 3.7.1 to keep the upcast active? \"needs to be aware of < 3.8.0\" — that word \"awareness\" suggests they thought the resolved triton would be below 3.8. The corresponding wheel turned out to be 3.8.0. There's ambiguity. But \"the wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index\" is the primary directive, and pip proved it's 3.8.0+git4cff872c. Also on the index, for rocm7.14.0, besides 3.8.0+git4cff872c there's only 3.7.1+git0263a6a6 — 3.7.1 conflicts with torch's declared dependency, so it can't be called the \"corresponding\" one without loosening torch's dependency (--no-deps = loosening). Ruling: use 3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0.\n\nUpdate the Containerfile's ARG TRITON_PIN and comment. Then rebuild. Note that the earlier layers are cached — pip will re-download. Also delete the failure receipt? build.sh will rewrite it at the end; receipts-verify during packaging tests on the second run: the failure receipt exists at the point tests run → test_receipts_verify_runs_clean FAILs → build.sh aborts before rebuild! Need to delete the failure receipt before rerun (or it gets overwritten later). Delete now."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"The build empirically resolved the true companion: **torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 declares `triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0`**. That is the exact companion wheel (my inference of 3.7.1 was wrong). I'll pin that and document the awareness of <3.8:\n\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dacad88afc6747fca1520cc4","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index —\n# verified by pip's own resolver: torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on exactly\n# triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (anything else is ResolutionImpossible).\n# < 3.8 awareness (IMPORTS.md): the fork's fp8-upcast gate keys on triton < 3.8,\n# so on this wheel the admission stands but the in-kernel upcast is bypassed —\n# fp8 dots ride triton 3.8's own lowering, and the fidelity checkpoint grades it.\nARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\"","oldText":"# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index — the\n# ROCm build of the triton 3.7.1 that torch 2.13.0 declares (git0263a6a6),\n# and it sits under the triton < 3.8 gate the fork's fp8-upcast keys on.\nARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0\""}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe/container/Containerfile"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent — it got resolved empirically: **torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0**. So the corresponding triton is 3.8.0+git4cff872c, not 3.7.1. But IMPORTS says \"needs to be aware of < 3.8.0: the fork's fp8-upcast gate is keyed on triton < 3.8.\" Hmm — if triton 3.8.0 is the exact corresponding wheel for torch 2.13.0, then the fp8-upcast gate `on_gfx1151() and triton < 3.8` evaluates to FALSE at runtime on this substrate, and the upcast won't happen!\n\nWait — this is an important finding. Options:\n1. Pin triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0 and install torch with --no-deps (or install triton first and then install torch, tolerating pip's conflict warning). But \"don't loosen anything: the torch pin must be exactly satisfied\" — the torch pin is satisfied; triton is a separate wheel. Installing torch in a state where pip warns about the dependency conflict… does pip install fail if you later install a conflicting package? Order: install triton 3.7.1 first, then `pip install torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 torchvision...` — pip checks the dependencies of the torch being installed: requires triton==3.8.0... → ResolutionImpossible again, because it validates against the installed environment. Workaround: first install torch alone with --no-deps… but then torch's other dependencies (rocm-sdk-core, sympy, networkx, etc.) won't be installed. Alternative: run `pip install --no-deps torch==... torchvision==... triton==3.7.1...`, then `pip install` the remaining runtime dependencies… but the list of torch's dependencies is unclear.\n\nHmm. Which is correct for the campaign? IMPORTS.md is authoritative: \"triton | wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index; fallback: the pytorch-triton-rocm wheel declared by torch 2.13.0 | same index | needs to be aware of < 3.8.0: the fork's fp8-upcast gate is keyed on triton < 3.8 (see PR #52970 pattern). Record the resolved version in the build receipt.\"\n\n\"The wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index\" — for torch 2.13.0, what AMD publishes as the corresponding wheel is 3.8.0+git4cff872c (which pip just proved). But then the gate `triton < 3.8` kills the fp8 upcast. Could it be that… the fork's gate is keyed on `triton < 3.8`, and 3.8.0+git4cff872c is parsed as version 3.8.0 → not less than 3.8. Hmm, so admission happens but the upcast is OFF? The admission patch approves the scheme; the upcast kernel transform is gated on triton<3.8. With triton 3.8, the kernel might work natively (does tl.dot support fp8 on newer triton? On RDNA3.5 there's no FP8 unit — the upcast exists because older triton lowers fp8 tl.dot incorrectly; newer triton might handle it fine, or AMD's triton might still need the upcast).\n\nWait, re-reading: \"the fork's fp8-upcast gate is keyed on triton < 3.8 (see PR #52970 pattern).\" #52970 applies the upcast when on_gfx1151 and triton < 3.8 — meaning in triton ≥ 3.8 the fp8 dot is properly handled in software? That's the upstream understanding: ROCm triton 3.8 got correct fp8 emulation on RDNA3.5? So the corresponding set (torch 2.13 + triton 3.8.0+git4cff872c) is coherent: with triton 3.8, the gate intentionally skips the upcast.\n\nBut wait — does the fork's patch still approve the MOE scheme on gfx1151 regardless of triton version? Yes, the approval is keyed on gfx1151; the upcast is conditioned on triton<3.8 (on 3.8, the fp8 dot path is assumed to be correct).\n\nHmm, but with the triton 3.8 wheel on RDNA3.5, is `tl.dot` on fp8 inputs actually numerically sound? That's UNKNOWN-1, and we resolve it via the proxy + fidelity checkpoint. The campaign spec/IMPORTS accepts the corresponding set; the gate handles both regimes.\n\nDecision: use the exact corresponding set that pip resolved: triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0. This is \"the wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index\" and satisfies torch's own declaration — the most defensible \"don't loosen anything\" stance. Record it in the receipt and comment about the < 3.8 awareness: at 3.8.0 the fork's upcast gate is false, and the approved fp8 dot goes through triton's own lowering; if fidelity is broken, it's UNKNOWN-1 territory.\n\nNo wait — one more consideration. If the upcast doesn't fire, then \"admission patch + upcast\" (world-first piece) goes untested… but that's campaign semantics beyond my task; my task: exact corresponding set, record the resolved version. The smoke receipt logs the admission verdict (approval), and that should pass.\n\nHmm, but hold on — could it be that the intent of IMPORTS was to choose triton 3.7.1 to keep the upcast active? \"needs to be aware of < 3.8.0\" — that word \"awareness\" suggests they thought the resolved triton would be below 3.8. The corresponding wheel turned out to be 3.8.0. There's ambiguity. But \"the wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index\" is the primary directive, and pip proved it's 3.8.0+git4cff872c. Also on the index, for rocm7.14.0, besides 3.8.0+git4cff872c there's only 3.7.1+git0263a6a6 — 3.7.1 conflicts with torch's declared dependency, so it can't be called the \"corresponding\" one without loosening torch's dependency (--no-deps = loosening). Ruling: use 3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0.\n\nUpdate the Containerfile's ARG TRITON_PIN and comment. Then rebuild. Note that the earlier layers are cached — pip will re-download. Also delete the failure receipt? build.sh will rewrite it at the end; receipts-verify during packaging tests on the second run: the failure receipt exists at the point tests run → test_receipts_verify_runs_clean FAILs → build.sh aborts before rebuild! Need to delete the failure receipt before rerun (or it gets overwritten later). Delete now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The build empirically resolved the true companion: **torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 declares `triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0`**. That is the exact companion wheel (my inference of 3.7.1 was wrong). I'll pin that and document the awareness of <3.8:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dacad88afc6747fca1520cc4","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index —\n# verified by pip's own resolver: torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on exactly\n# triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (anything else is ResolutionImpossible).\n# < 3.8 awareness (IMPORTS.md): the fork's fp8-upcast gate keys on triton < 3.8,\n# so on this wheel the admission stands but the in-kernel upcast is bypassed —\n# fp8 dots ride triton 3.8's own lowering, and the fidelity checkpoint grades it.\nARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\"","oldText":"# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index — the\n# ROCm build of the triton 3.7.1 that torch 2.13.0 declares (git0263a6a6),\n# and it sits under the triton < 3.8 gate the fork's fp8-upcast keys on.\nARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0\""}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe/container/Containerfile"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1808,"output":2271,"cacheRead":67584,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1647,"totalTokens":71663,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787984153306,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a1f468de-4145-41ae-9d87-0e79baa595be","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
