{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — but there's a real tension here. Let me reconsider. IMPORTS.md states that the resolved triton \"Must be < 3.8.0\". If the accompanying wheel is 3.8.0, then that statement in IMPORTS becomes stale/incorrect. But my lane's boundary condition says don't touch IMPORTS.md (only container/ and results/receipts/). The spec's P4 says \"stable-index torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 wheels — an exact pin for the fork\". Hmm — \"an exact pin for the fork\" — the fork's requirements/build/cuda.txt stays at 2.13.0.\n\nThe phrase \"Must be < 3.8.0 awareness\" can be read as \"Awareness is required: must be < 3.8.0\" — meaning awareness that the gate is keyed on < 3.8. If the resolved version is 3.8.0, then the upcast is disabled at runtime, and the admission patch's upcast (one of the two groundbreaking elements) goes untested. This is significant for the campaign.\n\nAlternative: Install triton 3.7.1+git0263a6a6 with --no-deps handling: install the trio with --no-deps, then use pip check to explicitly install the remaining dependencies? To satisfy torch's actual other dependencies (rocm-sdk-core, sympy, filelock, fsspec, jinja2, networkx, typing-extensions, numpy, mpmath — all hosted on the vendor index!). The vendor index is literally mirroring exactly torch's dependency set (filelock, fsspec, jinja2, markupsafe, mpmath, networkx, numpy, pillow, setuptools, sympy, typing-extensions — that's why those exist there!). So:\n\npip install --index-url ROCM_WHL --no-deps torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0\npip install --index-url ROCM_WHL rocm-sdk-core==7.14.0 filelock fsspec jinja2 networkx sympy typing-extensions numpy ...\n\nBut torchvision also has dependencies (numpy, pillow, torch satisfied). And \"don't relax anything\" — overriding torch's declared triton dependency is definitely a form of relaxation. And the smoke test's approval only checks the oracle's admission, not the state of the upcast.\n\nWhich does the campaign want? The task's goal states: \"install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and a matching triton wheel from the vendor's stable index ... (relax nothing: satisfy the torch pin exactly; add torchaudio or drop the audio extra)\". \"A matching triton wheel\" — matching = the one the torch set declares = 3.8.0+git4cff872c. IMPORTS states \"wheel accompanying the torch set on the same index; fallback: pytorch-triton-rocm wheel declared by torch 2.13.0\" — both point to what torch declares = 3.8.0+git4cff872c. The \"< 3.8 awareness\" note is guidance about recording the version and knowing about the gate — and I'm recording it.\n\nProceed with 3.8.0+git4cff872c (the exact accompanying set, zero relaxation), and document it. This is the defensible, empirically grounded choice. The gate semantics become a runtime behavior the checkpoint observes (UNKNOWN-1/3.2 smoke only checks admission).\n\nDelete the failed receipt and rerun the build.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5c3d6ab3449d4196a11168f4","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe && rm -f results/receipts/build.json && nohup bash container/build.sh > .build/build.log 2>&1 & echo \"pid=$!\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":4140,"output":934,"cacheRead":67584,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":839,"totalTokens":72658,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787984202137,"responseId":"chatcmpl-5288a782-9c27-44bf-bf46-6778776ec54a","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5c3d6ab3449d4196a11168f4","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"pid=69499\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787984223127}]}
