{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Hmm, the pip cache bind mount via `podman build -v` — writes during build happen as the build user (rootless → subuid). If the cache permissions get messed up, pip fails with a cache write error → but pip tolerates unreadable caches without issues. The first run writes as subuid root; the host user can't delete it later — it's tolerable since it's scratch.\n\nWait, one issue: the pip cache mount at /root/.cache/pip — the pip in the container is root, but in rootless builds it's mapped to subuid. Well, whatever.\n\nFirst delete the fail receipt, then re-run. The apt layer change invalidates the cache from STEP ~4 onward; wheels get re-downloaded (now they get cached into the pip cache mount for subsequent runs).\n"}}
