{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The ROCm root of `_rocm_sdk_core` doesn't contain the hip-lang CMake package. The hip-lang cmake config might be in `rocm-sdk-devel` or `rocm-sdk-libraries`. The index had `rocm-sdk-devel/`. AMD's wheel set for building from source: `rocm-sdk-devel` contains the hip compiler/cmake files. Let me check the contents of the rocm-sdk-devel wheel — install it and check. Actually, torch's LoadHIP.cmake searches ROCM_PATH for lib/cmake/hip-lang. On the wheel-based ROCm (amd's \"rocm\" pip meta-package), the typical build uses `pip install rocm-sdk-devel` (as AMD's TheRock/pytorch docker does: pytorch/rocm wheels include `rocm` + `rocm-sdk-core` for runtime, and `rocm-sdk-devel` for building).\n\nAlso note that pip installed `rocm-7.14.0`, `rocm-bootstrap`, `rocm-sdk-core`, and `rocm-sdk-libraries` as dependencies of torch. devel isn't pulled in automatically. Add `rocm-sdk-devel==7.14.0` (verify the pin naming on the index) explicitly to the substrate install.\n\nCheck the version listing on the index:"}}
