{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"GPU is detected (Radeon 8060S = gfx1151), but fp8 kernel launch fails with hipErrorInvalidImage — \"device kernel image is invalid\". Interesting. This is an e4m3fn zeros + cast kernel, a trivial torch elementwise op… does hipErrorInvalidImage mean the compiled kernel binary doesn't contain an ISA for gfx1151? The torch wheels are gfx1151 multi-arch… hmm. It might be a first-time JIT triton/inductor cache path issue, or a simple dtype cast kernel should be a precompiled hipblas/elementwise… the `x.to(bfloat16)+1` kernel is a torch-compiled elementwise CUDA kernel from the torch wheel — if invalid image, that means torch's bundled kernels don't have gfx1151 code?? But the wheel is advertised as gfx1151-capable (verified in the 2026-08-28 evidence: kyuz0's index).\n\nWait — maybe the issue is: this container lacks proper HSA/gfx detection environment. AMD's wheel torch usually requires env vars like HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION? No — the whole point of gfx1151 wheels is native support.\n\nLet me get more diagnostic info: run with AMD_LOG_LEVEL=3, or try a simpler op on cuda with default float32 to see whether any kernel works."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"GPU is seen but the first kernel launch fails. Let me diagnose:\n\n"}}
