{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Before rebuilding the whole image, I'll hot-patch the existing image to quickly verify the hypothesis (installing the 3 wheels and re-running the probe) — this will be faster. In reality, the rebuild is mostly cached except for the substrate layer (pip cache → fast), followed by the editable rebuild of vLLM (about 10 minutes using the ccache in .build/ccache… wait, ccache was mounted during the build — was it actually used? The build took 822 seconds wall-clock including tests. ccache stats? The editable rebuild re-runs anyway (since layers get invalidated from substrate onward). With ccache, compilation becomes fast.\n\nFirst, hot-patch verification:\npodman run -i --rm ... flashnext:dev pip install --index-url ... the 3 wheels? --rm → temporary. However, I can chain within the same container execution: pip install then probe with python. Let's run that."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Quick validation before rebuilding — hot-patch the current image with the device wheels in one run:\n\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_23dc365c39a24ab2b6dc5256","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp && podman run -i --rm --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host flashnext:dev bash -c '\npip -q install --index-url https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ \"amd-torch-device-gfx1151==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\" \"amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\" \"rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151==7.14.0\" &&\npython3 - <<\"PY\"\nimport torch\ny = torch.ones(4, device=\"cuda\") + 1\nprint(\"float32 kernel ok:\", y.cpu().tolist())\nz = torch.zeros(4, dtype=torch.float8_e4m3fn, device=\"cuda\")\nprint(\"fp8 cast ok:\", bool(((z.to(torch.bfloat16) + 1).sum().item()) == 4.0))\nfrom vllm.platforms import rocm\nprint(\"gcn_arch:\", rocm._GCN_ARCH)\nfrom vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.experts.triton_moe import TritonExperts\nfrom vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.utils.quant_utils import kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym\nok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym)\nprint(\"admitted:\", ok, \"|\", why)\nPY\n' 2>&1 | grep -vE \"^\\s*$\" | tail -15","timeout":900}}}}
