{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The fork hook returns a `bool`, not `(bool, reason)`. `scripts/run-smoke.sh` (the existing one, outside my scope) executes `ok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(...)` → TypeError → the admission item gets reported as FAIL, and the smoke receipt becomes fail. This is a latent defect in run-smoke.sh that affects the cp-smoke checkpoint. I can't fix scripts/run-smoke.sh (boundary: container/ and results/receipts/ only). Per the brief: \"If completion requires paths under the authority surface, return {\"outcome\":\"needs-authority\",\"paths\":[...]}.\" My task itself (container-recipe) does not require modifying run-smoke.sh, and its acceptance criteria pass. However, the delivered image will cause cp-smoke to fail due to this mismatch.\n\nOptions: (a) complete the task and flag the issue in the final message (as a note, or as needs-authority). The needs-authority result would block committing the work — the task itself is completable within the boundary; the smoke script issue belongs to a separate lane / operator. Complete the task, commit, and in the final message prominently mention the latent defect in run-smoke.sh (as information, not needs-authority, since my task's completion doesn't require that path). Hmm — but would it be better to return needs-authority to let the operator make the call? The brief says: \"If completion requires paths under the authority surface, return needs-authority.\" My completion does not require it. So: complete and note the finding.\n\nNext, rebuild the image with the device wheel baked in. The rebuild reuses the cache up through the substrate step; the substrate layer changes → re-execute; pip cache mount speeds it up. After that, re-verify that GPU probes pass with the baked-in image, and re-run build.sh as a whole to regenerate the receipt (currently stale — the receipt references the old image digest). Actually simpler: re-run build.sh wholesale (packaging tests + build + receipt). About 15 minutes total."}}
