{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Task complete. **Outcome: done** — committed `d89f338` on branch `tally-work/flashnext-824b68c09c23/container-recipe` (not pushed, per brief). All committed paths are inside the binding write boundary (`container/`, `results/receipts/`); `.build/` is local untracked cache scratch only.\n\n## What was delivered\n\n**`container/Containerfile`** — Ubuntu 24.04, py3.12 venv at `/opt/venv`, MIT credit header for kyuz0's `Dockerfile.ubuntu-repoamd` recipe shape. Substrate pinned from the vendor stable index: `torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0`, `torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0`, triton, `rocm-sdk-devel` (HIP compiler for the source build), torchaudio omitted. Fork `mecattaf/vllm@flashnext` cloned `--depth 1` and built from source (`--no-build-isolation`, `PYTORCH_ROCM_ARCH=gfx1151`, ccache auto-detected). `container/rootfs/` overlay COPYs into site-packages; `/opt/flashnext/build-info.json` records fork commit / torch / triton / build time. Iteration hooks: bind-mount a checkout over `/opt/vllm` + host ccache/pip caches.\n\n**`container/build.sh`** — packaging tests first → `podman build` tagged `flashnext:dev` → receipt `results/receipts/build.json` (fail status on any error via ERR trap).\n\n**Receipt banked and graded clean**: status `pass`, lane `container`, torch `2.13.0+rocm7.14.0`, triton `3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0`, fork `bdb6f042…`, wall-clock 839 s; `receipts-verify.py` → 0 violations. Acceptance criterion `recipe-pins` passes. **Verified on the GPU**: kernels launch, fp8 storage cast finite, `Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration` registered, and the fork's loud admission line fires (\"admitting block-FP8 fused MoE … on gfx1151 via in-kernel bf16 upcast\").\n\n## Findings the campaign should know\n\n1. **The exact companion triton is `3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0`** — pip proves torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 requires exactly it (3.7.1 is `ResolutionImpossible`). It sits *at*, not under, the fork's `triton < 3.8` upcast gate; the fork's admission log nonetheless reports the bf16 upcast path active. Recorded in the Containerfile comment and receipt.\n2. **Critical substrate finding**: the generic torch/torchvision wheels carry **no device kernels** — the first launch dies `hipErrorInvalidImage` until the device packs `amd-torch-device-gfx1151` / `amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151` / `rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151` are installed (torch loads them from `torch/.kpack/`). All three are now pinned in the recipe.\n\n## Two latent defects in pre-existing `scripts/run-smoke.sh` (outside my write boundary — left untouched, flagging for the operator/cp-smoke)\n\n- Its `podman run` lacks `-i`, so the heredoc python receives an empty stdin and exits 0 silently — no smoke receipt is ever written.\n- `admission()` unpacks `ok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(...)`, but the fork's hook returns a bare `bool` → `TypeError` → the admission check would grade FAIL even once `-i` is fixed."}}
