ine fires (\"admitting block-FP8 fused MoE … on gfx1151 via in-kernel bf16 upcast\").\n\n## Findings the campaign should know\n\n1. **The exact companion triton is `3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0`** — pip proves torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 requires exactly it (3.7.1 is `ResolutionImpossible`). It sits *at*, not under, the fork's `triton < 3.8` upcast gate; the fork's admission log nonetheless reports the bf16 upcast path active. Recorded in the Containerfile comment and receipt.\n2. **Critical substrate finding**: the generic torch/torchvision wheels carry **no device kernels** — the first launch dies `hipErrorInvalidImage` until the device packs `amd-torch-device-gfx1151` / `amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151` / `rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151` are installed (torch loads them from `torch/.kpack/`). All three are now pinned in the recipe.\n\n## Two latent defects in pre-existing `scripts/run-smoke.sh` (outside my write boundary — left untouched, flagging for the operator/cp-smoke)\n\n- Its `podman run` lacks `-i`, so the heredoc python receives an empty stdin and exits 0 silently — no smoke receipt is ever written.\n- `admission()` unpacks `ok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(...)`, but the fork's hook returns a bare `bool` → `TypeError` → the admission check would grade FAIL even once `-i` is fixed."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1108,"output":922,"cacheRead":100352,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":47,"totalTokens":102382,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787987330997,"responseId":"chatcmpl-58d06278-275b-4324-919d-3ae7cc7754d1","rawStopReason":"stop"}}
