 https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm flashnext","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2287,"output":279,"cacheRead":65536,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":66,"totalTokens":68102,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787984063169,"responseId":"chatcmpl-aa82a939-105c-4b72-ac4d-ee77ca0c6897","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_775a7499245c4d05ba174da9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ACCEPTANCE-PASS\nbdb6f0420e797de9266de593326368091085cc3b\trefs/heads/flashnext\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787984070595},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Acceptance criteria pass, fork exists. Next, run the actual build. This is the heavy part — could take 1–3 hours. Let me confirm that running the repo's tests first isn't currently broken: python3 -m unittest discover -s tests. Then launch the build in the background with nohup and monitor.\n\nActually, build.sh itself runs the tests first. Let me kick it off and tail it. Disk: 114G free; the torch wheel is about 2.5–3GB download, the image could grow to 20–30GB. OK.\n\nOne risk: podman build --volume in rootless mode: is it supported in podman build -v host:container (buildah)? Yes, `podman build --volume` has been supported since podman 3.x.\n\nAnother potential issue: Ubuntu base image pull — network should be fine.\n\nAnother risk: `pip install -e /opt/vllm --no-build-isolation` could take a long time to compile HIP sources (about 40–90 minutes on 32 cores), but that's fine.\n\nvLLM might require `git` during setup (setuptools-scm) for version retrieval — the .git directory exists (shallow clone) ✓.\n\nMAX_JOBS unset → ninja defaults to nproc; does setup.py cap it? Fine.\n\nStarting the build in the background.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Acceptance passes and the fork branch exists. Now launch the actual image build (the long part) in the background and monitor it.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9161cfebbc9242379c49c5d7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe && mkdir -p .build && nohup bash container/build.sh > .build/build.log 2>&1 & echo \"pid=$!\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":579,"output":421,"cacheRead":67584,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":300,"totalTokens":68584,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787984070600,"responseId":"chatcmpl-4a542992-a299-475d-86e6-6fc63dae996f","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9161cfebbc9242379c49c5d7","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"pid=64087\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787984082110},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — running build.sh will write results/receipts/build.json upon completion, and moreover the packaging test step gets executed. But note: build.sh runs `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` — in the current tree, only test_repo_invariants.py exists. Also, .build/ should be gitignored? .gitignore contains .engine-overlay/, result, etc., but no .build/. Should I not commit .build/? The conflictDomains are container + results/receipts; .build/ is outside the write boundary! \"All paths touched by any task commit must remain within them\" — touched by the *commit*. Untracked local scratch outside a commit is… well, it's safer to add it to .gitignore, but modifying .gitignore is outside the boundary. I just won't commit .build. But it's clutter. Alternatively, should I move logs/cache under container/.build? The ccache default is .build/ccache. Hmm — let's keep it simple: the scratch directory is untracked and never committed. That's acceptable.\n\nAlso note: if the build fails, the fail receipt gets written to results/receipts/build.json. If the final result isn't a pass, I won't commit that.\n\nMonitor the logs.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d7b0803ebc2240f7ab16a2f6","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe && sleep 60 && tail -20 .build/build.log && git status --porcelain","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1021,"output":359,"cacheRead":67584,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":261,"totalTokens":68964,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787984082115,"responseId":"chatcmpl-0617fe0d-b50c-4068-b956-5f05f36178c3","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d7b0803ebc2240f7ab16a2f6","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"  Installing build dependencies: finished with status 'done'\n  Getting requirements to build wheel: started\n  Getting requirements to build wheel: finished with status 'done'\n  Preparing metadata (pyproject.toml): started\n  Preparing metadata (pyproject.toml): finished with status 'done'\nINFO: pip is looking at multiple versions of torch to determine which version is compatible with other requirements. This could take a while.\nERROR: Cannot install torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0 because these package versions have conflicting dependencies.\n\nThe conflict is caused by:\n    The user requested triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0\n    torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\n\nTo fix this you could try to:\n1. loosen the range of package versions you've specified\n2. remove package versions to allow pip attempt to solve the dependency conflict\n\nERROR: ResolutionImpossible: for help visit https://pip.pypa.io/en/latest/topics/dependency-resolution/#dealing-with-dependency-conflicts\nError: building at STEP \"RUN pip install --index-url ${ROCM_WHL}         ${TORCH_PIN} ${TORCHVISION_PIN} ${TRITON_PIN}\": while running runtime: exit status 1\ncontainer/build.sh: FAILED — writing fail receipt\nbuild receipt (fail): /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe/results/receipts/build.json\n?? .build/\n?? container/\n?? results/receipts/build.json\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787984153300},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent — it got resolved empirically: **torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0**. So the corresponding triton is 3.8.0+git4cff872c, not 3.7.1. But IMPORTS says \"needs to be aware of < 3.8.0: the fork's fp8-upcast gate is keyed on triton < 3.8.\" Hmm — if triton 3.8.0 is the exact corresponding wheel for torch 2.13.0, then the fp8-upcast gate `on_gfx1151() and triton < 3.8` evaluates to FALSE at runtime on this substrate, and the upcast won't happen!\n\nWait — this is an important finding. Options:\n1. Pin triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0 and install torch with --no-deps (or install triton first and then install torch, tolerating pip's conflict warning). But \"don't loosen anything: the torch pin must be exactly satisfied\" — the torch pin is satisfied; triton is a separate wheel. Installing torch in a state where pip warns about the dependency conflict… does pip install fail if you later install a conflicting package? Order: install triton 3.7.1 first, then `pip install torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 torchvision...` — pip checks the dependencies of the torch being installed: requires triton==3.8.0... → ResolutionImpossible again, because it validates against the installed environment. Workaround: first install torch alone with --no-deps… but then torch's other dependencies (rocm-sdk-core, sympy, networkx, etc.) won't be installed. Alternative: run `pip install --no-deps torch==... torchvision==... triton==3.7.1...`, then `pip install` the remaining runtime dependencies… but the list of torch's dependencies is unclear.\n\nHmm. Which is correct for the campaign? IMPORTS.md is authoritative: \"triton | wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index; fallback: the pytorch-triton-rocm wheel declared by torch 2.13.0 | same index | needs to be aware of < 3.8.0: the fork's fp8-upcast gate is keyed on triton < 3.8 (see PR #52970 pattern). Record the resolved version in the build receipt.\"\n\n\"The wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index\" — for torch 2.13.0, what AMD publishes as the corresponding wheel is 3.8.0+git4cff872c (which pip just proved). But then the gate `triton < 3.8` kills the fp8 upcast. Could it be that… the fork's gate is keyed on `triton < 3.8`, and 3.8.0+git4cff872c is parsed as version 3.8.0 → not less than 3.8. Hmm, so admission happens but the upcast is OFF? The admission patch approves the scheme; the upcast kernel transform is gated on triton<3.8. With triton 3.8, the kernel might work natively (does tl.dot support fp8 on newer triton? On RDNA3.5 there's no FP8 unit — the upcast exists because older triton lowers fp8 tl.dot incorrectly; newer triton might handle it fine, or AMD's triton might still need the upcast).\n\nWait, re-reading: \"the fork's fp8-upcast gate is keyed on triton < 3.8 (see PR #52970 pattern).\" #52970 applies the upcast when on_gfx1151 and triton < 3.8 — meaning in triton ≥ 3.8 the fp8 dot is properly handled in software? That's the upstream understanding: ROCm triton 3.8 got correct fp8 emulation on RDNA3.5? So the corresponding set (torch 2.13 + triton 3.8.0+git4cff872c) is coherent: with triton 3.8, the gate intentionally skips the upcast.\n\nBut wait — does the fork's patch still approve the MOE scheme on gfx1151 regardless of triton version? Yes, the approval is keyed on gfx1151; the upcast is conditioned on triton<3.8 (on 3.8, the fp8 dot path is assumed to be correct).\n\nHmm, but with the triton 3.8 wheel on RDNA3.5, is `tl.dot` on fp8 inputs actually numerically sound? That's UNKNOWN-1, and we resolve it via the proxy + fidelity checkpoint. The campaign spec/IMPORTS accepts the corresponding set; the gate handles both regimes.\n\nDecision: use the exact corresponding set that pip resolved: triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0. This is \"the wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index\" and satisfies torch's own declaration — the most defensible \"don't loosen anything\" stance. Record it in the receipt and comment about the < 3.8 awareness: at 3.8.0 the fork's upcast gate is false, and the approved fp8 dot goes through triton's own lowering; if fidelity is broken, it's UNKNOWN-1 territory.\n\nNo wait — one more consideration. If the upcast doesn't fire, then \"admission patch + upcast\" (world-first piece) goes untested… but that's campaign semantics beyond my task; my task: exact corresponding set, record the resolved version. The smoke receipt logs the admission verdict (approval), and that should pass.\n\nHmm, but hold on — could it be that the intent of IMPORTS was to choose triton 3.7.1 to keep the upcast active? \"needs to be aware of < 3.8.0\" — that word \"awareness\" suggests they thought the resolved triton would be below 3.8. The corresponding wheel turned out to be 3.8.0. There's ambiguity. But \"the wheel that comes with the torch set from the same index\" is the primary directive, and pip proved it's 3.8.0+git4cff872c. Also on the index, for rocm7.14.0, besides 3.8.0+git4cff872c there's only 3.7.1+git0263a6a6 — 3.7.1 conflicts with torch's declared dependency, so it can't be called the \"corresponding\" one without loosening torch's dependency (--no-deps = loosening). Ruling: use 3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0.\n\nUpdate the Containerfile's ARG TRITON_PIN and comment. Then rebuild. Note that the earlier layers are cached — pip will re-download. Also delete the failure receipt? build.sh will rewrite it at the end; receipts-verify during packaging tests on the second run: the failure receipt exists at the point tests run → test_receipts_verify_runs_clean FAILs → build.sh aborts before rebuild! Need to delete the failure receipt before rerun (or it gets overwritten later). Delete now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The build empirically resolved the true companion: **torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 declares `triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0`**. That is the exact companion wheel (my inference of 3.7.1 was wrong). I'll pin that and document the awareness of <3.8:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dacad88afc6747fca1520cc4","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index —\n# verified by pip's own resolver: torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on exactly\n# triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (anything else is ResolutionImpossible).\n# < 3.8 awareness (IMPORTS.md): the fork's fp8-upcast gate keys on triton < 3.8,\n# so on this wheel the admission stands but the in-kernel upcast is bypassed —\n# fp8 dots ride triton 3.8's own lowering, and the fidelity checkpoint grades it.\nARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\"","oldText":"# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index — the\n# ROCm build of the triton 3.7.1 that torch 2.13.0 declares (git0263a6a6),\n# and it sits under the triton < 3.8 gate the fork's fp8-upcast keys on.\nARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\nARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0\""}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe/container/Containerfile"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1808,"output":2271,"cacheRead":67584,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1647,"totalTokens":71663,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787984153306,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a1f468de-4145-41ae-9d87-0e79baa595be","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dacad88afc6747fca1520cc4","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe/container/Containerfile."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  46 FROM docker.io/ubuntu:24.04\n  47 \n  48 ARG ROCM_WHL=https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/\n  49 # The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n- 50 # wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index — the\n- 51 # ROCm build of the triton 3.7.1 that torch 2.13.0 declares (git0263a6a6),\n- 52 # and it sits under the triton < 3.8 gate the fork's fp8-upcast keys on.\n+ 50 # wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index —\n+ 51 # verified by pip's own resolver: torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on exactly\n+ 52 # triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (anything else is ResolutionImpossible).\n+ 53 # < 3.8 awareness (IMPORTS.md): the fork's fp8-upcast gate keys on triton < 3.8,\n+ 54 # so on this wheel the admission stands but the in-kernel upcast is bypassed —\n+ 55 # fp8 dots ride triton 3.8's own lowering, and the fidelity checkpoint grades it.\n  53 ARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\n  54 ARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\n- 55 ARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0\"\n+ 58 ARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\"\n  56 \n  57 ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive\n  58 RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n  59         python3.12 python3.12-venv python3.12-dev \\\n     ...","patch":"--- /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe/container/Containerfile\n+++ /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe/container/Containerfile\n@@ -46,14 +46,17 @@\n FROM docker.io/ubuntu:24.04\n \n ARG ROCM_WHL=https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/\n # The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n-# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index — the\n-# ROCm build of the triton 3.7.1 that torch 2.13.0 declares (git0263a6a6),\n-# and it sits under the triton < 3.8 gate the fork's fp8-upcast keys on.\n+# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index —\n+# verified by pip's own resolver: torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on exactly\n+# triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (anything else is ResolutionImpossible).\n+# < 3.8 awareness (IMPORTS.md): the fork's fp8-upcast gate keys on triton < 3.8,\n+# so on this wheel the admission stands but the in-kernel upcast is bypassed —\n+# fp8 dots ride triton 3.8's own lowering, and the fidelity checkpoint grades it.\n ARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\n ARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\n-ARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0\"\n+ARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\"\n \n ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive\n RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n         python3.12 python3.12-venv python3.12-dev \\\n","firstChangedLine":50},"isError":false,"timestamp":1787984202132},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — but there's a real tension here. Let me reconsider. IMPORTS.md states that the resolved triton \"Must be < 3.8.0\". If the accompanying wheel is 3.8.0, then that statement in IMPORTS becomes stale/incorrect. But my lane's boundary condition says don't touch IMPORTS.md (only container/ and results/receipts/). The spec's P4 says \"stable-index torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 wheels — an exact pin for the fork\". Hmm — \"an exact pin for the fork\" — the fork's requirements/build/cuda.txt stays at 2.13.0.\n\nThe phrase \"Must be < 3.8.0 awareness\" can be read as \"Awareness is required: must be < 3.8.0\" — meaning awareness that the gate is keyed on < 3.8. If the resolved version is 3.8.0, then the upcast is disabled at runtime, and the admission patch's upcast (one of the two groundbreaking elements) goes untested. This is significant for the campaign.\n\nAlternative: Install triton 3.7.1+git0263a6a6 with --no-deps handling: install the trio with --no-deps, then use pip check to explicitly install the remaining dependencies? To satisfy torch's actual other dependencies (rocm-sdk-core, sympy, filelock, fsspec, jinja2, networkx, typing-extensions, numpy, mpmath — all hosted on the vendor index!). The vendor index is literally mirroring exactly torch's dependency set (filelock, fsspec, jinja2, markupsafe, mpmath, networkx, numpy, pillow, setuptools, sympy, typing-extensions — that's why those exist there!). So:\n\npip install --index-url ROCM_WHL --no-deps torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 triton==3.7.1+git0263a6a6.rocm7.14.0\npip install --index-url ROCM_WHL rocm-sdk-core==7.14.0 filelock fsspec jinja2 networkx sympy typing-extensions numpy ...\n\nBut torchvision also has dependencies (numpy, pillow, torch satisfied). And \"don't relax anything\" — overriding torch's declared triton dependency is definitely a form of relaxation. And the smoke test's approval only checks the oracle's admission, not the state of the upcast.\n\nWhich does the campaign want? The task's goal states: \"install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and a matching triton wheel from the vendor's stable index ... (relax nothing: satisfy the torch pin exactly; add torchaudio or drop the audio extra)\". \"A matching triton wheel\" — mat