odel":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1342,"output":488,"cacheRead":78848,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":271,"totalTokens":80678,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787984836504,"responseId":"chatcmpl-bbe9fc79-209d-427e-a222-3e98e20d08c0","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6515ce04993c4289977b9629","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"rocm_sdk_devel-7.14.0-py3-none-linux_x86_64.whl\nrocm_sdk_libraries-7.14.0-py3-none-linux_x86_64.whl\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787984850180},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"rocm-sdk-devel 7.14.0 exists. But where does it install hip-lang's cmake? Probably into the same `_rocm_sdk_core` tree? Hmm — the pip package layout for rocm-sdk-devel: installs into site-packages/_rocm_sdk_core (merging in development files)? AMD's wheel layout: rocm-sdk-core installs runtime into `_rocm_sdk_core/`, and rocm-sdk-devel also installs into `_rocm_sdk_core/` (adding cmake and headers). Yes, I think they share the `_rocm_sdk_core` namespace directory. Let's add `rocm-sdk-devel==7.14.0` to the substrate pip install line.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5cb431cf66984443b465f36e","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"ARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\"\n# The from-source engine build needs the HIP compiler + cmake packages, which\n# the runtime wheels do not pull in; devel files merge into _rocm_sdk_core.\nARG ROCM_DEVEL_PIN=\"rocm-sdk-devel==7.14.0\"","oldText":"ARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\""},{"newText":"RUN pip install --index-url ${ROCM_WHL} \\\n        ${TORCH_PIN} ${TORCHVISION_PIN} ${TRITON_PIN} ${ROCM_DEVEL_PIN}","oldText":"RUN pip install --index-url ${ROCM_WHL} \\\n        ${TORCH_PIN} ${TORCHVISION_PIN} ${TRITON_PIN}"}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/