 my own validation, I'll re-run smoke inline with -i. This is just a local probe, not a deliverable. The cp-smoke checkpoint has the same bug... but that's for the campaign to deal with (maybe their podman version behaves differently, or maybe the judge notices it). Hmm — should I report it? I could mention it in my summary. It's outside my authority to modify.\n\nAlright, let me try the smoke probe with -i.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"`podman run` needs `-i` to take the heredoc on stdin (a latent quirk in the pre-existing run-smoke.sh, which is outside my write boundary). Probing with `-i`:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_57b0751eeb9c40fda6129634","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/824b68c09c23/container-recipe && podman run -i --rm --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host flashnext:dev python3 - <<'PY'\nimport torch\nprint(\"torch\", torch.__version__)\nprint(\"cuda available:\", torch.cuda.is_available())\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    print(\"device:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n    x = torch.zeros(4, dtype=torch.float8_e4m3fn, device=\"cuda\")\n    print(\"fp8 alloc+cast ok:\", bool(((x.to(torch.bfloat16) + 1).sum().item()) == 4.0))\nfrom vllm.platforms import rocm\nprint(\"gcn_arch:\", rocm._GCN_ARCH)\nfrom vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.experts.triton_moe import TritonExperts\nfrom vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.utils.quant_utils import kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym\nok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym)\nprint(\"admitted:\", ok, \"|\", why)\nPY\necho \"exit=$?\"","timeout":600}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1254,"output":791,"cacheRead":84480,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":389,"totalTokens":86525,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"